\DOC SUBSUMED_ASSIGNS_TAC

\TYPE {SUBSUMED_ASSIGNS_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Proves goals of the form {ASSIGNS t subsumed ASSIGNS u} outright.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. Applied to a goal whose conclusion is a subsumption between
two {ASSIGNS} components, it closes the goal:
{
   ?- ASSIGNS t subsumed ASSIGNS u
   ========================================  SUBSUMED_ASSIGNS_TAC
}
\noindent In the observed traces it succeeds when the two components are
identical, or when the first denotes a part of the region denoted by the
second.

\FAILURE
In the observed traces it fails, with a matching error raised by an internal
rule application, when the two {ASSIGNS} components are unrelated — neither
identical nor one a part of the other — so no applicable subsumption rule
matches the conclusion.

\COMMENTS
All observed inputs are goals with no assumptions and of this subsumption
shape, and the only successful outcome seen is the goal being closed.

\ENDDOC
